  "description": "SUNKES crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C75 H103 La7 N18 O53,2(C1 H4 O1),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 10 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La3 (La) has 10 O neighbors; La4 (La) has 10 O neighbors; La5 (La) has 10 O neighbors; La6 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La7 (La) has 10 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.763-5.304 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.97-172.07°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [La7{(S)-L}6(CO3)(NO3)6(OCH3)(CH3OH)7]·2CH3OH·5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
